!!id:"https://tson.io/2026/39/m/meta-resolved.tn"
@doc:"""
  Resolver-output fixture for meta.tn, the kernel (2026 Revision 39
  draft). Parse the source schema, run the resolver, canonicalise,
  compare.

  A resolved form's header is its source's, and the kernel imports nothing,
  so this one carries its `!!id` alone and is read under the pre-loaded
  kernel. Nothing in the document marks it resolved; a processor reads it
  as a resolved form because its caller says so ([TSON-SCHEMA] Section
  8.1). The kernel's machinery is six schema maps nested as the root's
  entries `numeric`, `unicode`, `net`, `atom`, `meta` and `binary`, each
  written nested and tagged by its type's path, `!meta.schema`, each
  member named by its path (`meta.record`, `unicode.text_type`,
  `atom.ordering`); the vocabulary an author writes (`text`, `integer`,
  `bytes`, `doc`, `enum`, `set`, ...) and the synthetics it mints are the
  root's.

  Conventions:
  - Every entry is its value: a name maps to the body it resolves
    to, `!meta.record { ... }`, `!numeric.integer_type { ... }`,
    `!meta.alias { ... }`, `!meta.template { ... }`. Output is source with sugar
    expanded, bodies flattened and chains computed, and an entry
    written as a constructor application resolves to itself.
  - Fields at their default values are omitted (`optional: false`,
    `voidable: false`, `role: FREE`), and so are empty chains.
  - A type body carries `meta.type`'s one field, `chain`, a `meta.type_chain`.
    `supertypes` is the complete IS-A chain, every element a bare
    name, closed to a fixed point through applied parents; `subtypes`
    is its inverse over the entries of this map only (inverse edges
    from schemas that import this one are not represented here);
    `parents` is a record template's, the parents as written. Both
    name lists are written lexically sorted; a resolver's native
    ordering is implementation-defined, so comparison tools
    canonicalise both lists before comparing. Set-typed fields are
    compared as written, in source declaration order (Part 2
    Sections 7.5, 8). An empty chain is omitted.
  - An `!meta.alias` and a `!meta.template` compose `meta.top` and carry no
    chain.
  - A record's `fields` are flattened: a composition's fields are
    its operands' and its own, merged, so every record composing
    `meta.type` (through `atom`, `product` or `sum`) states `chain` among
    its fields first.
  - `meta.top`, `meta.type` and the three base kinds are `abstract`, so each
    states `extension: ABSTRACT`.
  - Source annotations are preserved in their authored positions,
    except `@doc`: a conforming resolver carries every source @doc
    verbatim, and these fixtures, which exist to be compared, leave
    entry docs out and substitute this conventions note for the
    document-level one.
  - Alias-kind names at type positions are stated as written: an
    alias is a hop, not a rewrite, so a use site naming an alias
    names the alias. A processor collapses the chain when it compiles
    readers, after linking, not in resolved output.
  - A slot that names a type (`meta.record_field.type`,
    `meta.tuple_element.element_type`, a container's type slots, choice
    variants, a parameter's `meta.type` and `bound`) is typed `meta.type_kind`,
    the kind of the types, and holds a bare name: a type's name,
    judged a member of the kind when the schema links. An
    application is a reference with an argument list, written
    unquoted in its canonical text, `result<T>`: no whitespace, and
    one space between arguments. A closed one lifts to an entry and is
    named bare, so one stands only where an application is still
    open: a record template's `parents` and field types, held text,
    and the `application` annotation.
  - The container constructors carry no parameters: their type
    slots are plain required `meta.type_kind`-typed fields, filled by the
    construction (or by a sugar form's desugaring) like any other
    required field. Within a template body `value` also carries a
    parameter, unlabelled: a token there is a parameter exactly when
    its text resolves into the enclosing entry's `parameters`
    (Part 2 Section 5.10's shadowing rule), and a closed entry has
    none for one to resolve into. A parametric `= P` is FIXED and
    `~ P` DEFAULT where it is written, the parameter in `value`;
    materialisation substitutes the argument into `value` and changes
    no other fact, and `optional` is the name's mark as written
    (Part 2 Section 5.7).
  - An argument is a reference or a token, positional against the
    head's parameters and typed where it lands: in a template body a
    parameter of either kind stands as its name, read against
    `parameters`.
  - An open entry is one of two values (Part 2 Sections 5.10, 8.1).
    A record template is a `!meta.record` with `parameters`, read as the
    vocabulary and not held: a parameter stands at a field's type, a
    field's value or an application's argument, and its `chain`
    holds `parents` as written, one of which may be an application.
    Every other open entry is held: a `!meta.template` carrying its
    `parameters` and, as text in `template`, the constructor
    application as written — a container as
    `!meta.array`/`!meta.map`/`!meta.tuple`/`!meta.choice`, an atom constructor as
    `!numeric.integer_type`, an alias as `!meta.alias` — unread until
    materialisation substitutes the parameters away. An entry that
    closes a template application carries the derived `@meta.application`
    at its schema-map key, the application it is the instantiation
    of, read as stated on ingest; none appear here, as nothing in
    this schema applies a non-constructor template.
  - Synthetic entries — the closed forms the sugar lifts to (Part 2
    Section 5.3) — are instances of the constructor they build, are
    referenced by the field that wrote the sugar, and carry the
    derived `@meta.synthetic` marker at their schema-map keys (Part 2
    Sections 6, 8.2); on ingest the marker is discarded and
    recomputed. Their internal names here follow the
    convention `<constructor>_<operands>_xxhash`, where the trailing
    `xxhash` is a placeholder for a content hash of the resolved
    binding record: the *shape* of the data — one internally named,
    `@meta.synthetic`-marked entry per distinct concrete form — is the
    conformance point; the hash spelling is an implementation's own
    business and the placeholder is deliberately not a real digest.
  - Bare parameter names (e.g. T) in bodies are read against the
    enclosing entry's `parameters` list.
  """
!schema {
  numeric => !meta.schema {
    integer_size => !meta.record { fields: {
      bits   => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.non_negative_integer }
      signed => !meta.record_field { type: boolean }
    } }

    integer_member_set => !meta.set_type { element_type: integer  min_items: 1 }

    integer_type => !meta.record { chain: { supertypes: [meta.atom meta.top meta.type] }  fields: {
      chain         => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
      size          => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.integer_size  optional: true }
      min           => !meta.record_field { type: integer  optional: true }
      exclusive_min => !meta.record_field { type: integer  optional: true }
      max           => !meta.record_field { type: integer  optional: true }
      exclusive_max => !meta.record_field { type: integer  optional: true }
      multiple_of   => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      members       => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.integer_member_set  optional: true }
    }
    groups: [
      !meta.field_group { members: [[min] [exclusive_min]]  optional: true }
      !meta.field_group { members: [[max] [exclusive_max]]  optional: true }
    ] }

    non_negative_integer => !numeric.integer_type { chain: { supertypes: [integer] }  min: 0 }
  }

  unicode => !meta.schema {
    text_member_set => !meta.set_type { element_type: text  min_items: 1 }

    text_type => !meta.record {
      chain: { supertypes: [meta.atom meta.top meta.type]  subtypes: [net.iri_type unicode.identifier_type unicode.regex_type] }
      fields: {
      chain         => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
      min_length    => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      max_length    => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      length        => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      pattern       => !meta.record_field { type: regex    optional: true }
      members       => !meta.record_field { type: unicode.text_member_set  optional: true }
      normalization => !meta.record_field { type: unicode.normalization  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: NONE }
    } }

    identifier_base => !enum { members: [XID ID ASCII NONE] }

    normalization => !enum { members: [NONE NFC NFKC NFKC_CASEFOLD ASCII_CASEFOLD] }

    identifier_type => !meta.record { chain: { supertypes: [atom.specification meta.atom meta.top meta.type unicode.text_type] }  fields: {
      chain         => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
      min_length    => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      max_length    => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      length        => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      pattern       => !meta.record_field { type: regex    optional: true }
      members       => !meta.record_field { type: unicode.text_member_set  optional: true }
      normalization => !meta.record_field { type: unicode.normalization  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: NFC }
      spec          => !meta.record_field { type: iri   optional: true  role: FIXED  value: "https://www.unicode.org/reports/tr31/" }
      start         => !meta.record_field { type: unicode.identifier_base  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: XID }
      continue      => !meta.record_field { type: unicode.identifier_base  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: XID }
      start_add     => !meta.record_field { type: text  optional: true }
      continue_add  => !meta.record_field { type: text  optional: true }
      medial        => !meta.record_field { type: text  optional: true }
      exclude       => !meta.record_field { type: text  optional: true }
    } }

    regex_type => !meta.record { chain: { supertypes: [atom.specification meta.atom meta.top meta.type unicode.text_type] }  fields: {
      chain         => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
      min_length    => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      max_length    => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      length        => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      pattern       => !meta.record_field { type: regex  optional: true }
      members       => !meta.record_field { type: unicode.text_member_set  optional: true }
      normalization => !meta.record_field { type: unicode.normalization  optional: true  role: FIXED  value: NONE }
      spec          => !meta.record_field { type: iri  optional: true  role: FIXED  value: "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9485" }
    } }
  }

  net => !meta.schema {
    scheme_set => !meta.set_type { element_type: net.scheme_name  min_items: 1 }

    scheme_name => !unicode.identifier_type { start: ASCII  continue: ASCII  continue_add: "+-."  exclude: "_"  normalization: ASCII_CASEFOLD }

    iri_type => !meta.record { chain: { supertypes: [atom.specification meta.atom meta.top meta.type unicode.text_type] }  fields: {
      chain          => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
      min_length     => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      max_length     => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      length         => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      pattern        => !meta.record_field { type: regex    optional: true }
      members        => !meta.record_field { type: unicode.text_member_set  optional: true }
      normalization  => !meta.record_field { type: unicode.normalization  optional: true  role: FIXED  value: NONE }
      spec           => !meta.record_field { type: iri      optional: true  role: FIXED  value: "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3987" }
      schemes        => !meta.record_field { type: net.scheme_set  optional: true }
      allow_relative => !meta.record_field { type: boolean  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: true }
      allow_fragment => !meta.record_field { type: boolean  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: true }
    } }
  }

  atom => !meta.schema {
    specification => !meta.record { chain: { subtypes: [net.iri_type unicode.identifier_type unicode.regex_type] }  fields: {
      spec => !meta.record_field { type: iri }
    } }

    ordering => @meta.annotation !enum { members: [NONE PARTIAL TOTAL] }

    bounded => @meta.annotation !meta.alias { target: boolean }

    exact => @meta.annotation !meta.alias { target: boolean }

    numeric => @meta.annotation !meta.alias { target: void }
  }

  meta => !meta.schema {
    top => !meta.record {
      chain: {
        subtypes: [binary.bytes_type enum meta.alias meta.array meta.atom meta.choice meta.declared_type meta.enum_type meta.map meta.namespace meta.product meta.record meta.reference meta.set_type meta.sum meta.template meta.tuple meta.type meta.value_type meta.void_type net.iri_type numeric.integer_type unicode.identifier_type unicode.regex_type unicode.text_type]
      }
      fields: {}
      extension: ABSTRACT
    }

    type_chain => !meta.record { fields: {
      parents    => !meta.record_field { type: array_type_kind_xxhash  optional: true }
      supertypes => !meta.record_field { type: array_type_kind_xxhash  optional: true }
      subtypes   => !meta.record_field { type: array_type_kind_xxhash  optional: true }
    } }

    type => !meta.record {
      chain: {
        supertypes: [meta.top]
        subtypes: [binary.bytes_type enum meta.array meta.atom meta.choice meta.declared_type meta.enum_type meta.map meta.namespace meta.product meta.record meta.reference meta.set_type meta.sum meta.tuple meta.value_type meta.void_type net.iri_type numeric.integer_type unicode.identifier_type unicode.regex_type unicode.text_type]
      }
      fields: {
        chain => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
      }
      extension: ABSTRACT
    }

    atom => !meta.record {
      chain: {
        supertypes: [meta.top meta.type]
        subtypes: [binary.bytes_type enum meta.enum_type meta.reference meta.value_type meta.void_type net.iri_type numeric.integer_type unicode.identifier_type unicode.regex_type unicode.text_type]
      }
      fields: {
        chain => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
      }
      extension: ABSTRACT
    }

    product => !meta.record { chain: { supertypes: [meta.top meta.type]  subtypes: [meta.array meta.map meta.namespace meta.record meta.set_type meta.tuple] }  fields: {
      chain          => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
      access_pattern => !meta.record_field { type: meta.product_access_type }
      size_type      => !meta.record_field { type: meta.product_size_type }
    }  extension: ABSTRACT }

    sum => !meta.record { chain: { supertypes: [meta.top meta.type]  subtypes: [meta.choice meta.declared_type] }  fields: {
      chain => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
    }  extension: ABSTRACT }

    namespace => !meta.record { chain: { supertypes: [meta.product meta.top meta.type] }  fields: {
      chain          => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
      access_pattern => !meta.record_field { type: meta.product_access_type  optional: true  role: FIXED  value: NAMED }
      size_type      => !meta.record_field { type: meta.product_size_type    optional: true  role: FIXED  value: VARIABLE }
      key_type       => !meta.record_field { type: meta.identifier_kind  optional: true }
      value_type     => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_kind }
      ordered        => !meta.record_field { type: boolean  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: false }
    } }

    alias => !meta.record { chain: { supertypes: [meta.top] }  fields: {
      target => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_kind }
    } }

    template_param => !meta.record { fields: {
      name  => !meta.record_field { type: meta.param_name }
      type  => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_kind }
      bound => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_kind  optional: true }
    } }

    template => !meta.record { chain: { supertypes: [meta.top] }  fields: {
      parameters => !meta.record_field { type: array_template_param_xxhash }
      template   => !meta.record_field { type: text }
    } }

    value_type => !meta.record { chain: { supertypes: [meta.atom meta.top meta.type] }  fields: {
      chain => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
    } }

    value => !meta.value_type {}

    void_type => !meta.record { chain: { supertypes: [meta.atom meta.top meta.type] }  fields: {
      chain => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
    } }

    identifier => !unicode.identifier_type { continue_add: "-" }

    type_name => !meta.alias { target: meta.identifier }

    field_name => !meta.alias { target: meta.identifier }

    param_name => !meta.alias { target: meta.identifier }

    product_access_type => !enum { members: [INDEX NAMED] }

    product_size_type => !enum { members: [FIXED VARIABLE] }

    field_role => !enum { members: [FREE DEFAULT FIXED] }

    record_extension_type => !enum { members: [ABSTRACT FINAL OPEN] }

    annotation => !meta.alias { target: void }

    synthetic => @meta.annotation !meta.alias { target: void }

    application => @meta.annotation !meta.alias { target: meta.type_kind }

    record_field => !meta.record { fields: {
      type     => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_kind }
      optional => !meta.record_field { type: boolean  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: false }
      voidable => !meta.record_field { type: boolean  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: false }
      role     => !meta.record_field { type: meta.field_role  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: FREE }
      value    => !meta.record_field { type: meta.value  optional: true }
    } }

    field_group => !meta.record { fields: {
      members          => !meta.record_field { type: array_array_text_1_c67f2b5e_1_xxhash }
      optional_members => !meta.record_field { type: array_text_1_xxhash  optional: true }
      optional         => !meta.record_field { type: boolean  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: false }
    } }

    field_map => !meta.namespace { value_type: meta.record_field  ordered: true }

    record => !meta.record { chain: { supertypes: [meta.product meta.top meta.type] }  fields: {
      chain          => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
      access_pattern => !meta.record_field { type: meta.product_access_type  optional: true  role: FIXED  value: NAMED }
      size_type      => !meta.record_field { type: meta.product_size_type    optional: true  role: FIXED  value: FIXED }
      fields         => !meta.record_field { type: meta.field_map }
      groups         => !meta.record_field { type: array_field_group_xxhash  optional: true }
      extension      => !meta.record_field { type: meta.record_extension_type  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: OPEN }
      discriminators => !meta.record_field { type: array_text_1_xxhash  optional: true }
      name_type      => !meta.record_field { type: meta.identifier_kind  optional: true }
      parameters     => !meta.record_field { type: array_template_param_xxhash  optional: true }
    } }

    array => !meta.record { chain: { supertypes: [meta.product meta.top meta.type]  subtypes: [meta.set_type] }  fields: {
      chain          => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
      access_pattern => !meta.record_field { type: meta.product_access_type  optional: true  role: FIXED  value: INDEX }
      size_type      => !meta.record_field { type: meta.product_size_type    optional: true  role: FIXED  value: VARIABLE }
      element_type   => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_kind }
      voidable       => !meta.record_field { type: boolean  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: false }
      ordered        => !meta.record_field { type: boolean  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: true }
      unique_items   => !meta.record_field { type: boolean  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: false }
      min_items      => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      max_items      => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.non_negative_integer  optional: true }
    } }

    set_type => !meta.record { chain: { supertypes: [meta.array meta.product meta.top meta.type] }  fields: {
      chain          => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
      access_pattern => !meta.record_field { type: meta.product_access_type  optional: true  role: FIXED  value: INDEX }
      size_type      => !meta.record_field { type: meta.product_size_type    optional: true  role: FIXED  value: VARIABLE }
      element_type   => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_kind }
      voidable       => !meta.record_field { type: boolean  optional: true  role: FIXED  value: false }
      ordered        => !meta.record_field { type: boolean  optional: true  role: FIXED  value: false }
      unique_items   => !meta.record_field { type: boolean  optional: true  role: FIXED  value: true }
      min_items      => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      max_items      => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.non_negative_integer  optional: true }
    } }

    map => !meta.record { chain: { supertypes: [meta.product meta.top meta.type] }  fields: {
      chain          => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
      access_pattern => !meta.record_field { type: meta.product_access_type  optional: true  role: FIXED  value: NAMED }
      size_type      => !meta.record_field { type: meta.product_size_type    optional: true  role: FIXED  value: VARIABLE }
      key_type       => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_kind }
      value_type     => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_kind }
      voidable       => !meta.record_field { type: boolean  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: false }
      ordered        => !meta.record_field { type: boolean  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: false }
      min_items      => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      max_items      => !meta.record_field { type: numeric.non_negative_integer  optional: true }
    } }

    tuple_element => !meta.record { fields: {
      element_type => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_kind }
      voidable     => !meta.record_field { type: boolean  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: false }
    } }

    tuple => !meta.record { chain: { supertypes: [meta.product meta.top meta.type] }  fields: {
      chain          => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
      access_pattern => !meta.record_field { type: meta.product_access_type  optional: true  role: FIXED  value: INDEX }
      size_type      => !meta.record_field { type: meta.product_size_type    optional: true  role: FIXED  value: FIXED }
      elements       => !meta.record_field { type: array_tuple_element_xxhash }
    } }

    tuple1 => !meta.template { parameters: [{ name: T  type: meta.type_kind }]  template: "!meta.tuple { elements: [{ element_type: T }] }" }

    voidable_tuple1 => !meta.template {
      parameters: [{ name: T  type: meta.type_kind }]
      template: "!meta.tuple { elements: [{ element_type: T  voidable: true }] }"
    }

    enum_set => !meta.set_type { element_type: text  min_items: 1 }

    enum_type => !meta.record { chain: { supertypes: [meta.atom meta.top meta.type]  subtypes: [enum] }  fields: {
      chain     => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
      name_type => !meta.record_field { type: meta.identifier_kind }
      members   => !meta.record_field { type: meta.enum_set }
    } }

    choice => !meta.record { chain: { supertypes: [meta.sum meta.top meta.type] }  fields: {
      chain    => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
      variants => !meta.record_field { type: array_type_kind_xxhash }
      disjoint => !meta.record_field { type: boolean  optional: true }
    } }

    disjoint => @meta.annotation !meta.alias { target: void }

    declared_type => !meta.record { chain: { supertypes: [meta.sum meta.top meta.type] }  fields: {
      chain => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
    } }

    declared => !meta.declared_type {}

    reference => !meta.record { chain: { supertypes: [meta.atom meta.top meta.type] }  fields: {
      chain => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
      of    => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_kind }
    } }

    kind => !meta.template { parameters: [{ name: T  type: meta.type_kind }]  template: "!meta.reference { of: T }" }

    identifier_kind => !meta.reference { of: unicode.identifier_type }

    atom_kind => !meta.reference { of: meta.atom }

    type_kind => !meta.reference { of: meta.type }

    ref => !meta.template { parameters: [{ name: T  type: meta.type_kind }]  template: "!meta.reference { of: T }" }

    schema => !meta.namespace { key_type: meta.type_name  value_type: meta.declared }
  }

  binary => !meta.schema {
    bytes_encoding => !enum { members: [BASE64 BASE64URL BASE32 HEX] }

    bytes_type => !meta.record { chain: { supertypes: [meta.atom meta.top meta.type] }  fields: {
      chain      => !meta.record_field { type: meta.type_chain  optional: true }
